cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use irradpy2 in published work, please cite it as below."
title: "irradpy2: Multi-source solar irradiance data acquisition, modeling, separation, and forecasting toolkit"
version: 1.0.10
date-released: 2026-08-18
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Lin
    given-names: Peiyu
keywords:
  - solar irradiance
  - meteorological data
  - data acquisition
  - clear-sky modeling
  - clear-sky detection
  - irradiance separation
  - solar forecasting
abstract: >-
  irradpy2 is a Python package for solar irradiance data acquisition,
  processing, modeling, separation, forecasting, and evaluation. It provides
  ground-based and gridded data downloaders, 62 clear-sky irradiance models,
  23 clear-sky detection methods, 7 irradiance separation models, and 5 GHI
  forecasting methods behind a consistent interface.
